  <h2>Installation Instructions</h2>

  <h3>Step 1</h3>
  <p>Download from <a href="http://inference.phy.cam.ac.uk/Dasher/downloads/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dasher website</a> or search for "Dasher" on the Android Market.</p>

  <h3>Step 2</h3>
  <p>Running Dasher will present a blank screen (titled Dasher) while Dasher loads (please wait). You'll then be presented with Dasher's own settings.</p>

  <p>The "Input Mode" page offers a choice of methods, e.g. "Touch Control" or "Tilt Control", of which you may pick one. (Each will bring up further settings specific to that mode.)</p>

  <h3>Step 3</h3>
  <p>Next you must enable Dasher as an input method. This varies between models. The following instructions are for a Nexus One running Android 2.1 (Eclair) or 2.2 (Froyo).</p>

  <h4>3a) From your desktop, press menu button, and choose "Settings"</h4>

  <h4>3b) Choose "Language & Keyboard"</h4>

  <h4>3c) A list of input methods should be displayed, including Dasher.</h4>
  <p>Make sure Dasher is enabled i.e. its box is ticked. (You will be warned about collecting data such as passwords. We do not recommend Dasher for entering passwords!)</p>

  <h3>Step 4</h3>
  <p>Exit from system settings, and select any text field to bring up your standard/previous input method.</p>

  <p>Long-press in the text field to pop-up menu and choose "Input Method".</p>

  <h3>Step 5</h3>
  <p>Select Dasher in the list of input methods.</p>

  <p>Dasher should then come up on your screen.</p>
